{"type":"text","timestamp":1788461581369,"sessionID":"ses_f97623cadffeAXH3306HGYPJy6","part":{"id":"prt_0689dfcb7001e5nmfY4bcN8qo2","messageID":"msg_0689dfbec001NnJvOLcZVJyVTF","sessionID":"ses_f97623cadffeAXH3306HGYPJy6","type":"text","text":"Let me verify the calculation logic step by step for the first test case:\n1. subtotal = 10.05\n2. discount_rate = 0.10 (10%)\n3. shipping = 2.00\n\nWith the corrected logic:\n1. discounted_subtotal = 10.05 * (1 - 0.10) = 10.05 * 0.90 = 9.045\n2. total_amount = 9.045 + 2.00 = 11.045\n3. money(11.045) = round(11.045, 2) = 11.05\n\nThis matches the expected result of 11.05, confirming our fix is correct.\n\nThe implementation now:\n1. Applies the customer discount to the subtotal before adding the shipping charge\n2. Rounds money values to two decimal places as required\n3. Passes all existing tests\n\n","time":{"start":1788461579447,"end":1788461581367}}}
